<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves discount rate at 1.00 pct after meeting.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves discount rate at 1.00 pct after meeting.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank (SNB) said it was keeping its discount rate unchanged at 1.00 percent after its regular weekly central bank board meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;I can tell you that there was no change,&quot; an SNB spokesman said.</p>
<p>The SNB last changed the rate when it was lowered to 1.00 percent from 1.50 percent on September 26.</p>
<p>No changes in the rate were expected by the market.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
